      "local_deviation": "A single supervised Local sidecar is not a multi-tenant resource pool. The native page must return this stable cloud-only disposition without emulating capacity or billing controls.",
      "judgment_rationale": "PoolDashboard calls tenant-scoped pool status, instance list, pause, resume, terminate and JSON metrics endpoints. The router enforces authentication, global administration, tenant scoping, cross-tenant 404 behavior, lifecycle conflicts and audit logging. Tenant scope intentionally withholds global capacity, so resource usage and prewarm remain degraded. Cloud Desktop now provides the native status, filtering, pagination, lifecycle and retry surface with the same stable degraded reason and without claiming unavailable capacity. Local Desktop stops before network, scope switching or module loading and returns cloud_runtime_pool_not_applicable because a single supervised sidecar is not a multi-tenant resource pool."
